+          "source_section": "Statement",
+          "quote": "Assume countable choice. If $P$ is Polish and $\\mu$ is a Borel probability measure on $P$, then for every Borel $A\\subseteq P$ and $\\varepsilon>0$ there is a compact $K\\subseteq A$ with $\\mu(A\\setminus K)<\\varepsilon$.",
